id: pm-gh1553
title: Rebase concurrent history assignments and removals without losing events
description: "External report from pm-web using pm-cli 2026.10.19: history merge refuses scalar rebase when main closes an item and a branch appends comments/field edits. Reproduce on current SDK before changing the fail-closed replay contract; a manually unioned stream passing health alone is not proof that event semantics are lossless."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[3]: context-management,"gh:1553",sdk
created_at: "2026-10-23T06:27:49.281Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-24T22:08:31.530Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-24T22:04:25.478Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-24T22:04:25.478Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Current-version fixture reproduces or disproves the reported event sequence; Each scalar transition and retained event is checked against strict replay; Any safe correction preserves hash/replay integrity and provides actionable refusal evidence.
parent: pm-o2kc
risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "Preserve validated whole-field history intent across concurrent deletion, including repeated removals and collection changes; retain strict nested/conditional refusal with typed event and pointer coordinates."
expected_result: "Concurrent closure, claim replacement, release and comments preserve every valid event and yield a strict verified history; ambiguous nested or conditional intent remains explicit."
actual_result: "Original pm-web 16-event histories merge and verify. Seven scalar regressions pass, including mixed satisfied removals plus comments; its negative control failed with before_hash_mismatch before cloning. Final 36-test focused cohort and linked item runs pass. The canonical full suite passed 11,222 tests and exact 100/100/100/100 before the two targeted review/alias corrections, each separately proven. Final-head hosted gates remain mandatory for PR1578."
